NNAAMMEE
     ppoowweerrdd — system power control utility

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppoowweerrdd [--aa _m_o_d_e] [--bb _m_o_d_e] [--ii _p_e_r_c_e_n_t] [--MM _f_r_e_q] [--mm _f_r_e_q] [--NN]
            [--nn _m_o_d_e] [--PP _p_i_d_f_i_l_e] [--pp _i_v_a_l] [--rr _p_e_r_c_e_n_t] [--ss _s_o_u_r_c_e] [--vv]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppoowweerrdd utility monitors the system state and sets various power con‐
     trol options accordingly.  It offers power-saving modes that can be indi‐
     vidually selected for operation on AC power or batteries.

     mmaaxxiimmuumm     Choose the highest performance values.  May be abbreviated as
                 mmaaxx.

     mmiinniimmuumm     Choose the lowest performance values to get the most power
                 savings.  May be abbreviated as mmiinn.

     aaddaappttiivvee    Attempt to strike a balance by degrading performance when the
                 system appears idle and increasing it when the system is
                 busy.  It offers a good balance between a small performance
                 loss for greatly increased power savings.  May be abbreviated
                 as aaddpp.

     hhiiaaddaappttiivvee  Like aaddaappttiivvee mode, but tuned for systems where performance
                 and interactivity are more important than power consumption.
                 It increases frequency faster, reduces frequency less aggres‐
                 sively, and will maintain full frequency for longer.  May be
                 abbreviated as hhaaddpp.

     The default mode is aaddaappttiivvee for battery power and hhiiaaddaappttiivvee for the
     rest.

     ppoowweerrdd recognizes these runtime options:

     --aa _m_o_d_e     Selects the _m_o_d_e to use while on AC power.

     --bb _m_o_d_e     Selects the _m_o_d_e to use while on battery power.

     --ii _p_e_r_c_e_n_t  Specifies the CPU load percent level when adaptive mode
                 should begin to degrade performance to save power.  The de‐
                 fault is 50% or lower.

     --MM _f_r_e_q     Specifies the maximum frequency to throttle up to.

     --mm _f_r_e_q     Specifies the minimum frequency to throttle down to.

     --NN          Treat "nice" time as idle for the purpose of load calcula‐
                 tion; i.e., do not increase the CPU frequency if the CPU is
                 only busy with "nice" processes.

     --nn _m_o_d_e     Selects the _m_o_d_e to use normally when the AC line state is
                 unknown.

     --PP _p_i_d_f_i_l_e  Specifies an alternative file in which the process ID should
                 be stored.

     --pp _i_v_a_l     Specifies a different polling interval (in milliseconds) for
                 AC line state and system idle levels.  The default is 250 ms.

     --rr _p_e_r_c_e_n_t  Specifies the CPU load percent level where adaptive mode
                 should consider the CPU running and increase performance.
                 The default is 75% or higher.

     --ss _s_o_u_r_c_e   Enforces method for AC line state refresh; by default, it is
                 chosen automatically.  The set of valid methods is ssyyssccttll,
                 ddeevvdd and aappmm (i386 only).

     --vv          Verbose mode.  Messages about power changes will be printed
                 to stdout and ppoowweerrdd will operate in the foreground.

FFIILLEESS
     /var/run/powerd.pid  The default PID file.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
