HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ppoowweerrdd utility first appeared in FreeBSD 6.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     Colin Percival first wrote eessttccttrrll, the utility that ppoowweerrdd is based on.
     Nate Lawson then updated it for cpufreq(4), added features, and wrote
     this manual page.

BBUUGGSS
     The ppoowweerrdd utility should also power down idle disks and other components
     besides the CPU.

     If ppoowweerrdd is used with _/_e_t_c_/_r_c_._d_/_p_o_w_e_r___p_r_o_f_i_l_e, they may override each
     other.

     The ppoowweerrdd utility should probably use the devctl(4) interface instead of
     polling for AC line state.

